========================================================================
THE JOIN LAW  (dominance composition as the 'addition' operator)
========================================================================
Testing H(T1 => T2) vs H(T1), H(T2) for small reps:
   H(1)⇒H(1) [n=3+3] = 1   (prod=1, sum=2)  =prod
   H(1)⇒H(3) [n=3+3] = 3   (prod=3, sum=4)  =prod
   H(3)⇒H(1) [n=3+3] = 3   (prod=3, sum=4)  =prod
   H(3)⇒H(3) [n=3+3] = 9   (prod=9, sum=6)  =prod
   H(1)⇒H(1) [n=4+3] = 1   (prod=1, sum=2)  =prod
   H(1)⇒H(3) [n=4+3] = 3   (prod=3, sum=4)  =prod
   H(3)⇒H(1) [n=4+3] = 3   (prod=3, sum=4)  =prod
   H(3)⇒H(3) [n=4+3] = 9   (prod=9, sum=6)  =prod
   H(5)⇒H(1) [n=4+3] = 5   (prod=5, sum=6)  =prod
   H(5)⇒H(3) [n=4+3] = 15   (prod=15, sum=8)  =prod

